From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TurboVadim <yolkin.vadim@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:15:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Reuse path search tables and mutable block positions

Lease a flat table until evaluator completion, including the main-to-worker
handoff for Leaf async paths. Synchronize free-list ownership transfers and
bound retention to 16 tables of at most 65536 cells. Clear node references
before pooling so unused cells cannot retain older cameFrom chains.
Keep Node.createHash identity, including collisions, and allocate fresh
nodes so returned paths remain unchanged when a table is reused.

Cache floor heights only for loaded, static shapes in synchronous searches;
async invalidation disables even preparation-time entries. Reuse block
positions and swim neighbor storage, and reconstruct paths by appending and
reversing. Preserve live step-height reads, EnumSet evaluator overrides, all
neighbor/cache reads and their order, heap operations and float arithmetic.

Ten focused tests pass. Differential validation covers 3258 randomized
searches, 17971709 trace entries, paths/reached flags, both RNG streams,
hazards/tags, hash collisions and concurrent/async searches.

Measured jointly with the preceding region change, six runs per jar:
mob-farm 2.264 to 1.985 mspt, -12.34% with a 95% half-width of 5.31 percentage
points; allocation 1998.841 to 1503.839 KB/tick, -24.76% +/-8.78 points.
Villager allocation falls from 638.146 to 600.151 KB/tick, -5.95% +/-1.30
points; its -2.05% timing change is inside the +/-2.30-point bound.

